From: Logan Saunders <32494494+RealMrLogan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:45:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] klippy: assorted Sovol host changes

On master, kept: gcode_shell_command (get_ip.cfg's _GET_IP), klippy:start_print, M24's busy check, the end-of-file position, the tip codes and SHAPER_CALIBRATE TEST=1's saved frequencies. Dropped: the chelper no-rebuild hunk (Klipper rebuilds c_helper.so; the printer has gcc), configfile's hidden config log, fixed -backup name and firmware_restart, toolhead's timing constants (moved upstream), listing hidden files, and GET_GCODE_STATE/SOVOL_GET_STATE, which nothing calls.

Power-loss recovery is not carried over: on every G1 from a file with X, Y and Z (each z-hop travel) it reread saved_variables.cfg and fsynced ~/sovol_plr_height, blocking Klipper's reactor up to 1.4 s and shutting the toolhead down with 'Timer too close' at layer 12 of a Benchy (2026-11-17; Sovol had disabled that check). To be redone off the reactor (UPSTREAMS.md, Later).
